---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../../shared/config/config";

const siteTitle = "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform";
---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle={siteTitle}
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Relapse After 7 Days — Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  description="What community members report about relapsing after about a week without pornography use."
  canonical="/relapse/after-7-days/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "About Relapse", url: "/relapse/" },
    { name: "After 7 days", url: "/relapse/after-7-days/" },
  ]}
>
  <h1>Relapse After 7 Days</h1>
  <p>Some community members describe a relapse after about a week of not using pornography.
  This page reports what they describe, without making any causal claim about timing.</p>

  <h2>What members report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Some describe the first week as a period of strong, frequent urges, and a relapse
    during that week as common.</li>
    <li>Members often link an early relapse to a specific trigger — stress, boredom, or
    being alone at night — rather than to a lack of effort.</li>
    <li>Several describe the first week as the hardest, with urges becoming more manageable
    afterward for those who continued.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What this means</h2>
  <p>A relapse at around seven days is not a meaningful clinical marker. There is no
  established timeline, and no evidence that seven days is a particular threshold. The
  pattern some members describe is simply that the early period is often difficult.</p>

  <p class="note">Treat an early relapse as information about your triggers, not as failure.
  See <a href="/relapse/recovery-after-relapse/">recovering after a relapse</a> and
  <a href="/patterns/early-days-hardest/">the early-days pattern</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
